('127.243.d.5.A',4,'Under sales law, a sale of goods is the transfer of title to goods for:','["no reason", "a favor", "a price", "free"]'::jsonb,2,'A sale requires price.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.B',3,'Certain sales contracts must be in writing under the:','["tax law", "bailment rule", "tort law", "statute of frauds"]'::jsonb,3,'Large sales often need writing.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.B',4,'A sale of goods above a certain dollar amount generally must be:','["in a signed writing", "hidden", "verbal", "oral only"]'::jsonb,0,'The statute of frauds applies.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.C',3,'Ownership of goods moving from seller to buyer is a:','["lien", "transfer of title", "tort", "warranty"]'::jsonb,1,'Title is legal ownership.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.C',4,'Risk of loss shifts to the buyer when:','["prices change", "the weather changes", "title or delivery terms say so", "the seller sleeps"]'::jsonb,2,'Contract terms decide risk.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.D',3,'A seller''s promise that a product will work as stated is a:','["lien", "tariff", "deposit", "warranty"]'::jsonb,3,'Warranties guarantee quality.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.D',4,'Which warranty is automatically implied that goods are fit for ordinary use?','["implied warranty of merchantability", "service warranty", "lifetime warranty", "express warranty"]'::jsonb,0,'Merchantability is implied by law.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.E',3,'A student researching a sale-of-goods dispute can find cases on:','["rumors", "online legal research sites", "ads", "social posts"]'::jsonb,1,'Online sources provide cases.','original'),
('127.243.d.5.E',4,'When citing a sales case, a student should include:','["only a nickname", "a rumor", "the case name, court, and year", "a photo"]'::jsonb,2,'Citations make sources clear.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.A',3,'A check, a note, or a draft that can be transferred to another person is a:','["warranty", "deed", "tort", "negotiable instrument"]'::jsonb,3,'Negotiable instruments are transferable.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.A',4,'Negotiable instruments are used as a substitute for:','["money", "goods", "stock", "land"]'::jsonb,0,'They stand in for cash.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.B',3,'To be negotiable, an instrument must be in writing, signed, and contain an unconditional promise to:','["perform a service", "pay a fixed amount of money", "deliver goods", "sell land"]'::jsonb,1,'Negotiability requires fixed amount.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.B',4,'An instrument payable ''to bearer'' or ''to order'' meets the requirement of:','["a deed", "a lien", "payable to order or bearer", "a warranty"]'::jsonb,2,'Words of negotiability are needed.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.C',3,'A written promise by one person to pay another a sum of money is a:','["draft", "warranty", "check", "promissory note"]'::jsonb,3,'A note is a two-party promise.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.C',4,'An order by one person telling another to pay a third party is a:','["draft", "lease", "note", "deed"]'::jsonb,0,'Drafts are orders to pay.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.D',3,'Transferring a negotiable instrument by signing it over is:','["fraud", "negotiation", "default", "discharge"]'::jsonb,1,'Negotiation transfers rights.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.D',4,'When a debt on an instrument is paid and liability ends, this is:','["transfer", "negotiation", "discharge", "endorsement"]'::jsonb,2,'Discharge cancels liability.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.E',3,'A person who takes an instrument in good faith and for value is a:','["drawee", "cosigner only", "debtor", "holder in due course"]'::jsonb,3,'HDCs have special protections.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.E',4,'A holder in due course generally takes the instrument:','["free of most defenses", "without value", "with no rights", "subject to all defenses"]'::jsonb,0,'HDCs are protected.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.F',3,'Forgery and fraud are examples of:','["warranties", "defenses against payment", "deeds", "leases"]'::jsonb,1,'Defenses may block collection.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.F',4,'A real defense that works even against a holder in due course is:','["minor mistake", "slow delivery", "forgery", "late fee"]'::jsonb,2,'Real defenses are strong.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.G',3,'To research negotiable instrument cases, a student can use:','["rumors", "opinions", "ads", "online legal databases"]'::jsonb,3,'Cases are in databases.','original'),
('127.243.d.6.G',4,'A good source for case law on checks is:','["official court decisions", "social media", "coupons", "tabloids"]'::jsonb,0,'Official sources are reliable.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.A',3,'A person who is authorized to act for another is an:','["tenant", "agent", "principal", "competitor"]'::jsonb,1,'Agents act on behalf of principals.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.A',4,'An agency is usually created by:','["accident", "taxation", "agreement between principal and agent", "inheritance only"]'::jsonb,2,'Agreement forms agency.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.B',3,'An agency ends when the agent''s task is complete or when:','["it rains", "a holiday arrives", "the agent sleeps", "the principal revokes authority"]'::jsonb,3,'Principals can terminate.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.B',4,'An agent who exceeds authority may be:','["personally liable", "immune", "rewarded", "paid extra"]'::jsonb,0,'Acting beyond authority has consequences.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.C',3,'The relationship in which one person hires another to work for pay is:','["bailor-bailee", "employer-employee", "buyer-seller", "landlord-tenant"]'::jsonb,1,'Employment is a work relationship.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.C',4,'An employer controls how, when, and where the work is done for an:','["partner", "independent contractor", "employee", "shareholder"]'::jsonb,2,'Control signals employment.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.D',3,'Laws that protect workers from discrimination and unsafe conditions give employees:','["liens", "taxes", "fees", "rights"]'::jsonb,3,'Employee rights are protected.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.D',4,'An employee''s right to a safe workplace is protected by:','["OSHA", "FDIC", "FTC", "SEC"]'::jsonb,0,'OSHA sets safety standards.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.E',3,'Minimum wage and overtime rules come from:','["trust law", "labor legislation", "contract warranty", "bailment law"]'::jsonb,1,'Labor laws govern wages.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.F',3,'To research employment law cases, students can use:','["ads", "rumors", "online legal resources", "memes"]'::jsonb,2,'Databases contain cases.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.F',4,'When comparing two employment cases, a student should note:','["the clerk''s name", "the room", "only the date", "the facts and the court''s ruling"]'::jsonb,3,'Facts and rulings matter.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.A',3,'A business owned and run by one person with unlimited personal liability is a:','["sole proprietorship", "corporation", "trust", "partnership"]'::jsonb,0,'One owner, unlimited liability.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.A',4,'One advantage of a sole proprietorship is:','["shared profits", "easy to start and full control", "limited liability", "stock sales"]'::jsonb,1,'Simplicity and control.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.B',3,'Two or more people who agree to carry on a business together form a:','["corporation", "franchise", "partnership", "trust"]'::jsonb,2,'Partnerships share ownership.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.B',4,'A written agreement among partners is called a:','["warranty", "bailment", "draft", "partnership agreement"]'::jsonb,3,'It sets roles and shares.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.C',3,'A business that is a separate legal entity from its owners is a:','["corporation", "partnership", "bailment", "sole proprietorship"]'::jsonb,0,'Corporations are separate.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.C',4,'A corporation is formed by filing:','["a lease", "articles of incorporation", "a will", "a draft"]'::jsonb,1,'Articles create the corporation.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.D',3,'Owners of a corporation hold:','["drafts", "leases", "shares of stock", "warranties"]'::jsonb,2,'Stock represents ownership.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.D',4,'Shareholders'' liability for corporate debts is generally:','["double", "none", "unlimited", "limited to their investment"]'::jsonb,3,'Limited liability protects owners.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.E',3,'A board of directors helps:','["manage the corporation", "set taxes", "print money", "write laws"]'::jsonb,0,'Boards oversee management.','original'),
('127.243.d.8.E',4,'When a corporation ends and its assets are sold to pay debts, this is:','["merger", "dissolution", "incorporation", "formation"]'::jsonb,1,'Dissolution winds up a corporation.','original'),
('127.243.d.9.A',3,'Insurance works by spreading:','["taxes", "profits", "risk among many policyholders", "debts to one person"]'::jsonb,2,'Pooling risk is the principle.','original'),
('127.243.d.9.A',4,'The amount paid regularly for an insurance policy is the:','["deductible", "benefit", "claim", "premium"]'::jsonb,3,'Premiums buy coverage.','original'),
('127.243.d.9.B',3,'Insurance that covers damage to your home is:','["property insurance", "auto insurance", "life insurance", "health insurance"]'::jsonb,0,'Property policies cover buildings.','original'),
('127.243.d.9.B',4,'Life insurance pays a benefit when the insured:','["changes jobs", "dies", "moves", "sells a car"]'::jsonb,1,'Life policies pay on death.','original'),
('127.243.d.9.C',3,'A bond that protects an employer from employee theft is a:','["deed", "draft", "fidelity bond", "mortgage"]'::jsonb,2,'Fidelity bonds cover dishonesty.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_40_v1'
