('127.241.d.3.A',5,'A nation where prices and output are mostly set by buyers and sellers, with some government regulation, has what type of economy?','["pure command economy", "pure traditional economy", "mixed economy", "barter-only economy"]'::jsonb,2,'Mixed economies blend markets and government roles.','original'),
('127.241.d.9.D',5,'A customer''s deposit of $200 appears in her records but not yet on the bank statement. What is the best reconciliation step?','["Ignore it", "Subtract it from her records", "Close the account", "Add it to the statement balance as a deposit in transit"]'::jsonb,3,'Deposits in transit are added to the bank balance.','original'),
('127.243.d.1.A',5,'A company advertises a recalled toy as safe after learning of choking hazards. This conduct is best described as:','["unethical and potentially illegal", "acceptable puffery", "ethical marketing", "routine promotion"]'::jsonb,0,'Concealing hazards violates ethics and consumer law.','original'),
('127.243.d.7.E',5,'A law that bars employers from retaliating against workers who report unsafe conditions is an example of:','["a tax rule", "labor legislation protecting employees", "a trust provision", "a real estate statute"]'::jsonb,1,'Whistleblower protections are labor law.','original')
